   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam GB</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lifesaving Response to Returnees and Refugees from Sudan, South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will provide rapid emergency Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) response to at least 10,000 refugees and returnees in Renk (7,000) and Melut (3,000) Transit Centres. Emergency WASH infrastructure and services will be developed/installed  to meet critical WASH needs and work towards sustainable solutions by linking humanitarian interventions to long -term measures. The interventions will include emergency water trucking, pipeline extension from the existing distribution networks (Melut), construction of communal water points/tap stands, water treatment, and water quality monitoring. Oxfam will work closely with the county governments and water utility companies (for both Melut and Renk) in water service provision.</narrative>
  </description>
